# =============================================================================
# ISO 10218:2025 to IEC 62443 CROSSWALK, v0.1.0
# Kampakis and Co Ltd, trading as The Tesseract Academy. CC BY 4.0.
#
# Instance data for the RSSC vocabulary. Asserts the mappings between the two
# parts of ISO 10218:2025, the machinery security bridge IEC TS 63074:2023,
# and the IEC 62443 series, organised so that they can be filtered by the
# three-band autonomy gradient.
#
# MATCH DISCIPLINE
#   skos:exactMatch    = the two terms denote the same thing with no scope
#                        difference. NOT USED ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE. Across a
#                        safety and security boundary the scopes always differ
#                        at least in the party addressed, so asserting exact
#                        identity would be false precision.
#   skos:closeMatch    = a strong correspondence: the two clauses are about the
#                        same property of the same object, differing in the
#                        party addressed or in generality.
#   skos:relatedMatch  = the connection is real but the scopes cross rather
#                        than nest. Used wherever one side is a machinery
#                        requirement and the other a control-system property
#                        that the machinery requirement depends on.
#   skos:broadMatch /  = not used. No pair below stands in a clean genus and
#   skos:narrowMatch     species relation.
#
# EVIDENCE DISCIPLINE, AND THE POINT OF THE ARTEFACT
#   This file is AUDITABLE, NOT AUTHORITATIVE. Two kinds of assertion are kept
#   strictly apart:
#     * Assertions carrying ev:PublishedPreview record a correspondence that a
#       standards body itself lays out in structure that is published free.
#       Only the seven-row IEC TS 63074 clause 5.2 spine qualifies.
#     * Assertions carrying ev:AnalyticalInference are OURS. No standards body
#       asserts them. They are the reasoned join between a safety clause and a
#       security requirement, and a reader who disagrees can discard them
#       without discarding the cited facts underneath.
#   ev:NormativeReference is used NOWHERE in this file, deliberately. See the
#   REJECTED MAPPINGS block at the foot: the published normative-reference
#   lists of both parts of ISO 10218:2025 were read in full and neither
#   IEC TS 63074 nor any part of IEC 62443 appears in either of them.
#
# PAYWALL CONSTRAINT, TREATED AS A DESIGN FEATURE
#   No normative text from any ISO or IEC standard is reproduced here. Every
#   clause identifier, clause title, requirement identifier, requirement title,
#   edition and cover date below was read in the issuing body's own free
#   preview (cover page, contents, foreword, scope, normative references) and
#   is cited as a fact. Titles are published free. Requirement bodies are not,
#   and are not reproduced. A reader can therefore check every identifier in
#   this file without buying anything.
#
# SEPARATOR SUBSTITUTION
#   Official ISO and IEC titles separate title elements with U+2014 (ISO) or
#   U+2013 (IEC). House style forbids both characters. Titles appear here in
#   the BSI and EN full-stop rendering. The separator is the only alteration
#   made to any official title.
#
# INDEPENDENCE
#   Independent, self-initiated open research. Not endorsed by, affiliated
#   with or approved by ISO, IEC, CEN, CENELEC, BSI, ISA, the ISA Security
#   Compliance Institute, KAN, SGS or any other body named within it.
# =============================================================================

<https://tesseract.academy/id/rssc/crosswalk/iso10218-iec62443> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:title "ISO 10218:2025 to IEC 62443 crosswalk" ;
    dcterms:description "Reified, cited mappings binding the cybersecurity and safety-function clauses of ISO 10218-1:2025 and ISO 10218-2:2025 to the machinery security bridge IEC TS 63074:2023 and to the requirements of the IEC 62443 series, filtered by a three-band autonomy gradient, with per-band control gaps." ;
    dcterms:creator "Fabio Rovai" ;
    dcterms:creator "Kampakis and Co Ltd, trading as The Tesseract Academy" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:created "2026-08-08"^^xsd:date ;
    owl:imports <https://tesseract.academy/ns/rssc> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://tesseract.academy/ns/rssc> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .

